  },
  "static_dynamic_variables": null,
  "system_vs_user": null,
  "current_practice_gaps": [
    {
      "gap": "Reusable expertise now ships as first-class Agent Skills (SKILL.md), not only slash commands",
      "why": "The lesson encodes reusable prompts as .claude/commands/*.md slash commands and reusable behavior as sub-agents. Modern Claude Code adds Agent Skills — SKILL.md with frontmatter, progressive disclosure, and on-demand discovery — as the current idiom for packaging reusable engineering so it's discoverable and shareable. The seven-levels vocabulary maps 1:1 onto Skill bodies; the packaging has upgraded. The 'self-improving Expertise' idea also overlaps with today's memory/knowledge-file patterns.",
      "yt_topic": "RAW Agentic Coding: Zero to Agent SKILL / Agent Skills"
    },
    {
      "gap": "Course-era model ids are pinned in metadata (claude-opus-4-1-20250805)",
      "why": "quick-plan.md and background.md hard-code model: claude-opus-4-1-20250805, and the README aliases/metaprompt default to sonnet/opus generically. Current model families have moved on (Opus 4.8, Sonnet 5, Haiku 4.5, Fable 5). The Metadata section's model field is exactly where you'd swap these; treat pinned ids as period detail and pick the current best model at run time.",
      "yt_topic": "Claude model updates / picking the right model"
    },
    {
      "gap": "Background/headless delegation has hardened into the Claude Agent SDK + richer headless flags",
      "why": "background.md shells out to `claude --print --append-system-prompt … --dangerously-skip-permissions --output-format text` with run_in_background. That still works and is the clearest teaching form, but production delegation now uses the Claude Agent SDK (Python/TypeScript), structured --output-format json/stream-json, session resume, permission modes, and typed hooks — which is exactly what AH-3 (Claude Code SDK) builds toward. Same concept (agent as callable component, append vs overwrite system prompt), richer machinery.",
      "yt_topic": "Claude Code SDK / headless agents / building your own agent"
    },
    {
      "gap": "Parallel delegation now has worktree isolation and first-class background tasks",
      "why": "parallel_subagents.md fires N Task sub-agents in one batch — still valid — but current practice adds git-worktree isolation for agents that mutate files concurrently, plus background task orchestration and multi-agent workflow tooling. A modern reader should know the delegation ceiling is far higher (dozens of isolated agents) than the single-batch Task fan-out shown here. AH-4 (the O-agent / multi-agent orchestration) scales exactly this.",
      "yt_topic": "Parallel agents / multi-agent orchestration"
    },
    {
      "gap": "Doc-scraping via Firecrawl MCP is one option among several context-loading patterns",
      "why": "load_ai_docs.md depends on the Firecrawl MCP server (with a WebFetch fallback). Current Claude Code has broader native web tooling and MCP options, and the 'load docs into ai_docs/ for agents to read' pattern is one instance of the R&D (Reduce/Delegate) context engineering from AH-1. Concept is durable; the specific MCP dependency and the 24-hour TTL are implementation detail.",
      "yt_topic": "Context engineering / MCP / ai_docs pattern"
    }
  ],
