  "confidence_notes": [
    "Transcript is auto-generated; corrected readings used throughout: 'team at a prompt workflow' = t_metaprompt_workflow; 'plan byte view' / 'plan Vue view' = plan_vite_vue (Plan Vite Vue); 'crud' = CRUD; 'ZTE' = the zero-touch-engineering North Star from TAC; 'AFK agents' and 'ADWs' are TAC concepts.",
    "TIER LIST GRADES ARE HIGH-CONFIDENCE: every section/format position was derived from Dan's spoken grade AND cross-verified pixel-by-pixel against the completed on-screen grid in frame t2740-final-tier-list.jpg (~45:40). All 13 sections + 7 formats reconciled with zero conflicts.",
    "entities.ts defines 13 section entities, but prime_tier_list.md's inline doc comment says 'The 12 gradable entities' — a documentation drift (it predates '## High Level Prompt' being split out as its own entity). The README 'Agentic Prompt Sections' list also enumerates 12 (it folds High Level Prompt into the Title/Purpose group). The canonical count for the tier list is 13 sections.",
    "t_metaprompt_workflow.md capture-vs-code detail: on video the purpose reads 'follow the `Instructions`'; Dan says on camera 'this should be follow the workflow'; the shipped file on disk reads 'follow the `Workflow`'. The codebase is the corrected/final version. Frame t2280 shows the pre-correction video state (accurate to the recording).",
    "The README documents a `{{variable_name}}` reference syntax for Variables, but the actual prompt files reference variables by bare NAME (e.g. PATH_TO_PLAN, USER_PROMPT) inside backticks — the models resolve either. Minor doc-vs-practice inconsistency, noted for accuracy.",
    "Video duration 3441s (57:21) at 1920x1080/15fps (ffprobe + recording.json agree within ~1s). Quote timestamps cross-checked against the VTT and accurate to ~a few seconds; section-placement timestamps taken from VTT anchors.",
    "codebase_map covers all committed files; specs/, adws/, agentic_drop_zone/, generated ai_docs/*.md, settings.local.json, and metaprompt-generated commands are runtime artifacts (confirmed absent from the committed tree via git ls-files scope). CLAUDE.md exists but is effectively empty.",
    "yt_overlay_candidates have video_id: null / needs_id_verification: true — this brief supplied NO seed ID list (unlike tac-1), so IDs were deliberately NOT fabricated. Titles/mappings are accurate to known IndyDevDan themes and the lesson's own cross-references; Codex/Hermes must source and verify real IDs from the channel before publishing overlay links.",
    "current_practice_gaps written against Claude Code as of mid-2026 (Agent Skills, Agent SDK, worktrees, model families); the models axis in particular moves fast — revisit at publish time.",
    "Cross-references to sibling lessons resolved: 'elite/extended context engineering' = AH-1 (rd-framework-context-window-mastery); 'third agentic horizon extended lesson / Claude Code SDK' = AH-3 (building-domain-specific-agents); multi-agent scaling = AH-4 (the O-agent)."
  ],
  "codebase_map": {
    "root_readme": "README.md — the authoritative lesson spine: the 7 levels (each with required/secondary sections + example prompts), the ordered Agentic Prompt Sections catalog with descriptions, a full System Prompts vs User Prompts writeup (with comparison table and which-sections-work-best guidance), and a set of Claude Code bash aliases (cld/cldp/cldo/cldys/lfg/…).",
    "the_app": {
      "path": "apps/prompt_tier_list/",
      "what": "The on-screen 'AGENTIC PROMPT TIER LIST' — a Vite + Vue 3 + TypeScript drag-and-drop 5x5 grid (X: Beginner→Expert skill, Y: Useful→Useless). Entities are dragged from a pool into tier cells; this is the app Dan grades live and that start.md / prime_tier_list.md boot and prime.",
      "key_files": {
        "src/constants/entities.ts": "GRADABLE_ENTITIES — the definitive 13 section blocks (# Title, ## High Level Prompt, ## Metadata, ## Purpose, ## Variables, ## Instructions, ## Relevant Files, ## Codebase Structure, ## Workflow, ## Expertise, ## Template, ## Examples, ## Report) + 7 format files (high_level/workflow/higher_order/control_flow/delegate/template_metaprompt/self_improving).",
        "src/App.vue": "Main app; coordinates the grid and the entity pool.",
        "src/components/TierGrid.vue": "5x5 grid + axis labels (grid size constant lives here).",
        "src/components/GridCell.vue": "Individual cells with stacking/reordering.",
        "src/components/EntityPool.vue": "The 'SECTIONS & FORMATS' drag source.",
        "src/components/DraggableEntity.vue": "Individual draggable section/format chips.",
        "src/composables/useDragAndDrop.ts": "Native HTML5 drag/drop logic with JSON transfer.",
        "src/types/index.ts": "Entity / GridPosition / DragData interfaces.",
        "src/assets/global.css": "Dracula-inspired theme via CSS variables.",
        "index.html / package.json / vite.config.ts / tsconfig*.json / bun.lock": "Vite + Bun scaffolding."
      }
    },
    "prompts_by_level": {
      "L1_high_level": [
        ".claude/commands/all_tools.md — Title + high-level prompt: read your system prompt and list all tools in TS-signature format.",
        ".claude/commands/start.md — Title + Purpose + high-level prompt: cd apps/prompt_tier_list; bun install; bun run dev; open localhost:5173."
      ],
      "L2_workflow": [
        ".claude/commands/prime.md — description metadata; Workflow (git ls-files; read README.md); Report. The minimal workflow prompt.",
        ".claude/commands/prime_cc.md — prime variant: Run (execute prime.md top to bottom) + Read (.claude/**) + Report; a Claude-Code-focused prime.",
        ".claude/commands/prime_tier_list.md — Title + Purpose + Codebase Structure (context map, 'do not read') + rich Workflow ('read these files exclusively', IMPORTANT) + Report; no metadata.",
        ".claude/commands/quick-plan.md — metadata (model: claude-opus-4-1-20250805) + Variables (USER_PROMPT: $1 dynamic, PLAN_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY: `specs/` static) + Instructions + Workflow + Report (writes a plan spec)."
      ],
      "L3_control_flow": [
        ".claude/commands/build.md — metadata (Read,Write,Bash); Variables (PATH_TO_PLAN: $ARGUMENTS); Workflow line 17 early-return ('If no PATH_TO_PLAN, STOP immediately'); Report (git diff --stat).",
        ".claude/commands/build_w_report.md — build variant whose Report emits a structured YAML work_changes format (shows the Report/output section shaping response format).",
        ".claude/commands/create_image.md — metadata (Replicate MCP); Variables ($1/$2 positional + static MODEL google/nano-banana, ASPECT_RATIO 16:9); Workflow with prerequisite STOP conditionals + an <image-loop> XML loop; Report.",
        ".claude/commands/edit_image.md — Replicate via direct curl; Variables; Workflow with a loop + STOP conditionals (token/base64 checks); NO Report section (output format intentionally omitted)."
      ],
      "L4_delegate": [
        ".claude/commands/parallel_subagents.md — Variables (PROMPT_REQUEST: $1, COUNT: $2); Workflow: parse → DESIGN self-contained sub-agent prompts → launch N via Task in one batch → collect & summarize.",
        ".claude/commands/load_ai_docs.md — Variables (DELETE_OLD_AI_DOCS_AFTER_HOURS: 24 static); Workflow loops URLs in ai_docs/README.md and calls @agent-docs-scraper via Task per URL; Report Format (✅/❌ url → path).",
        ".claude/commands/background.md — metadata (model: claude-opus-4-1-20250805); Variables ($1 prompt, $2 model default sonnet, $3 report-file); Instructions; Workflow fires a full `claude` CLI instance with --append-system-prompt, --print, --dangerously-skip-permissions, run_in_background=true; writes a live progress report file."
      ],
      "L5_higher_order": [
        ".claude/commands/build.md — reused: passes a plan FILE in as PATH_TO_PLAN; top-level structure stays constant while the plan changes.",
        ".claude/commands/load_bundle.md — Variables (BUNDLE_PATH: $ARGUMENTS); reads a context-bundle JSONL, dedupes file entries, and re-reads files with their original parameters to reconstruct a prior agent's context (pairs with the context_bundle_builder hook)."
      ],
      "L6_template_metaprompt": [
        ".claude/commands/t_metaprompt_workflow.md — 'MetaPrompt': Variables (HIGH_LEVEL_PROMPT: $ARGUMENTS); Documentation (context map of Claude Code slash-command docs, web-fetched first); ## Specified Format template the agent fills in to emit a new Level-2 workflow prompt. (On-screen the purpose reads 'follow the Instructions'; Dan corrects it live to 'Workflow' and the shipped file says Workflow.)",
        ".claude/commands/plan_vite_vue.md — a rapid-prototyping meta prompt: Variables + Instructions + Workflow (bun create vite … --template vue-ts) + Codebase Structure + a large ## Plan Format template with conditional <if…> blocks; Report returns only the plan path."
      ],
      "L7_self_improving": [
        ".claude/commands/experts/cc_hook_expert/cc_hook_expert_plan.md — a hook-expert planner with a big dynamic ## Expertise section (Claude Code hook file structure, events, execution model, security). The self-improving example shown on screen.",
        ".claude/commands/experts/cc_hook_expert/cc_hook_expert_build.md — the paired builder that implements hook specs (its Expertise is updated by the _improve prompt).",
        ".claude/commands/experts/cc_hook_expert/cc_hook_expert_improve.md — the improvement mechanism: reviews recent hook changes and rewrites ONLY the ## Expertise sections of _plan and _build, leaving Workflows stable. This is 'the agent that updates the agent.'"
      ]
    },
    "sub_agents_system_prompts": {
      ".claude/agents/docs-scraper.md": "Sub-agent (system prompt) used by load_ai_docs: fetches a URL via Firecrawl/WebFetch and writes clean markdown to ai_docs/. Purpose + static OUTPUT_DIRECTORY + Workflow + strict Report format. Dan's canonical 'sub-agent system prompt' example (no dynamic vars beyond the prompt passed in).",
      ".claude/agents/meta-agent.md": "Sub-agent that GENERATES new sub-agent config files from a description (model: opus) — a meta pattern at the agent level, with its own Output Format template.",
      ".claude/agents/crypto-coin-analyzer.md": "Bonus domain sub-agent (paired with crypto_research.md / crypto_coin_analyzer_agent_prompt.md); not featured in the lesson narrative."
    },
    "config_and_hooks": {
      ".claude/settings.json": "Hooks-based settings (no flat permission allowlist): universal_hook_logger.py on every event (PreToolUse/PostToolUse/UserPromptSubmit/Stop/SubagentStop/Notification/PreCompact/SessionStart/SessionEnd) + context_bundle_builder.py on Read|Write and UserPromptSubmit. Referenced by the cc_hook_expert.",
      ".claude/hooks/universal_hook_logger.py": "Logs every hook event (the 'universal logger' the cc_hook_expert cites as a discovered pattern).",
      ".claude/hooks/context_bundle_builder.py": "Builds the context bundles that load_bundle.md consumes.",
      ".claude/output-styles/": "5 output styles (concise-done/tts/ultra, verbose-bullet-points/yaml-structured) — reusable response formats.",
      ".claude/utils/": "llm/ (anth.py, oai.py, ollama.py) and tts/ (elevenlabs, openai, pyttsx3) helper scripts used by hooks/agents.",
      "ai_docs/README.md": "The URL list load_ai_docs scrapes (Claude Code SDK headless, MCP, slash-commands, sub-agents, hooks, models, UV scripts).",
      "scripts/bg_claude_code_test.sh": "Shell harness for testing the background-agent pattern.",
      ".env.sample / .mcp.json.*.sample": "API-key placeholder and sample MCP configs (Replicate 28k, Firecrawl 7k, Playwright 10k) — token-budget-annotated MCP servers."
    },
    "generated_or_runtime_not_committed": {
      "specs/": "Plan output directory written by quick-plan.md / plan_vite_vue.md — created at runtime, not committed.",
      "ai_docs/*.md (scraped)": "load_ai_docs writes claude-code-hooks.md, claude-code-mcp.md, etc. at runtime (visible in the video's explorer); only ai_docs/README.md is committed.",
      "agentic_drop_zone/": "Image input/output zones referenced by create_image.md / edit_image.md — runtime only.",
      "adws/ and apps/{app_name}/": "Referenced by plan_vite_vue.md as targets for generated ADW scripts and new apps — created at runtime.",
      "settings.local.json / .claude/commands/<generated>.md": "Local overrides and metaprompt-generated commands — produced during use.",
      "CLAUDE.md": "Present but effectively empty (no committed project instructions)."
    }
  }
}
