+          <div class="checkpoint"><strong>Evidence:</strong> include the one-line variable diff, generated <code>prd/</code> path, and a one-sentence explanation of why the metadata description stayed stale.</div>
+          <div class="lab-box__pass"><h4>Pass criteria</h4><ul><li>All eight variables are classified correctly.</li><li>The operational path changes from one static-value edit.</li><li>The student does not falsely claim every textual reference updates.</li></ul></div>
+        </section>
+
+        <section class="lab-box" id="lab-run">
+          <span class="graded-badge">Checkpoint 4 · 20 points</span>
+          <h3 class="lab-box__title">Trigger Levels 1–4</h3>
+          <ul class="lab-box__meta"><li>20 minutes</li><li>Four observable runs</li><li>No external service</li></ul>
+          <ol class="lab-box__steps">
+            <li><strong>L1:</strong> run <code>/all_tools</code>. Verify a TypeScript-signature tool inventory.</li>
+            <li><strong>L2:</strong> run <code>/prime</code>. Verify it performs the Workflow’s two observations: <code>git ls-files</code> and <code>README.md</code>.</li>
+            <li><strong>L3:</strong> run <code>/build</code> with no argument. Verify line 17 stops immediately and asks for <code>PATH_TO_PLAN</code>.</li>
+            <li><strong>L4:</strong> run <code>/parallel_subagents "audit .claude/commands and report each listed prompt's level" 3</code>. Verify three self-contained prompts are authored and launched in one batch, then synthesized.</li>
+          </ol>
+          <div class="checkpoint"><strong>Evidence:</strong> preserve one complete sentence written by the primary agent as a prompt for a sub-agent. Annotate the context, scope, and output expectation it contains.</div>
+          <div class="lab-box__pass"><h4>Pass criteria</h4><ul><li>All four runs exhibit the predicted capability.</li><li>The L3 run stops rather than guessing.</li><li>The L4 run proves prompt authorship and synthesis, not just three outputs.</li></ul></div>
+        </section>
+
+        <section class="lab-box" id="lab-meta">
+          <span class="graded-badge">Checkpoint 5 · 15 points</span>
+          <h3 class="lab-box__title">Use Level 6 to generate a Level 2</h3>
+          <ul class="lab-box__meta"><li>15 minutes</li><li>Generated course command</li><li>Exact format review</li></ul>
+          <p>Run:</p>
+          <div class="terminal"><div class="terminal__bar"><span class="terminal__dot"></span><span class="terminal__dot"></span><span class="terminal__dot"></span></div><pre><code>/t_metaprompt_workflow "a prompt that lists every TODO comment under a dynamic search root and writes them to todos.md"</code></pre></div>
+          <ol class="lab-box__steps">
+            <li>Verify the generated file lands in <code>.claude/commands/</code> with a sensible name.</li>
+            <li>Verify metadata → title → purpose → Variables → Workflow → Report.</li>
+            <li>The invocation deliberately requests a dynamic search root, so Variables should be present. In the general template, Variables may be omitted when no variable is requested.</li>
+            <li>Verify there is a real sequential Workflow and no unrequested extra <code>## Instructions</code> section.</li>
+            <li>Notice the shipped template’s purpose sentence mentions Instructions although the Specified Format does not include that H2. Grade the generated structure by the Workflow and Specified Format rules.</li>
+          </ol>
+          <div class="checkpoint"><strong>Evidence:</strong> submit the generated headings, variables in dynamic-then-static order, and one paragraph explaining why this is a Level-2 output produced by a Level-6 prompt.</div>
+          <div class="lab-box__pass"><h4>Pass criteria</h4><ul><li>The output is a reusable command.</li><li>Its sections match the requested specified format.</li><li>Its Workflow is executable top to bottom.</li><li>No extra section appears because of stale wording.</li></ul></div>
+        </section>
+
+        <section class="lab-box" id="lab-stretch">
+          <h3 class="lab-box__title">Stretch · three transfer drills</h3>
+          <ul class="lab-box__meta"><li>Optional</li><li>Read before edit</li><li>Still course-only</li></ul>
+          <ol class="lab-box__steps">
+            <li><strong>Promote Level 2 → 3:</strong> add a missing-README STOP guard to a copy of <code>prime.md</code>. Change no other section.</li>
+            <li><strong>Trace Level 7:</strong> inspect the hook expert triplet and quote the instructions that say “ONLY Expertise” while workflows remain stable.</li>
+            <li><strong>Classify system scope:</strong> inspect <code>.claude/agents/docs-scraper.md</code>; list its Purpose, static output directory, Workflow, and Report/Response, then explain why its narrow role tolerates a more specific system prompt.</li>
+          </ol>
+        </section>
+
+        <h3>Scoring rubric · 100 points</h3>
+        <div class="rubric-grid" aria-label="Lab grading rubric">
+          <div class="rubric-head">Dimension</div><div class="rubric-head">Exemplary</div><div class="rubric-head">Competent</div><div class="rubric-head">Developing</div><div class="rubric-head">Missing</div>
+          <div>Setup + axes · 10</div><div>Reset proven; axes exact</div><div>App + axes correct</div><div>Direction confused</div><div>No evidence</div>
+          <div>Twenty-entity grid · 20</div><div>20/20 + reasons</div><div>18–19 correct</div><div>14–17 correct</div><div>&lt;14 correct</div>
+          <div>Prompt classification · 20</div><div>All with line evidence</div><div>One weak proof</div><div>Several guessed</div><div>No audit</div>
+          <div>Variables · 15</div><div>Syntax + drift explained</div><div>Classes and path correct</div><div>One misconception</div><div>No run</div>
+          <div>Levels 1–4 runs · 20</div><div>Four capabilities evidenced</div><div>Four runs present</div><div>One run incomplete</div><div>Multiple missing</div>
+          <div>Level-6 generation · 15</div><div>Exact format + reasoning</div><div>Valid Level-2 output</div><div>Extra/missing section</div><div>No artifact</div>
+        </div>
+
+        <aside class="callout callout--why">
+          <p class="callout__label">Pass threshold</p>
+          <p><strong>80/100 plus all safety invariants:</strong> no work outside the course repository; <code>/build</code> with no input must stop; the twenty-entity count must be correct; and the generated command must contain a real Workflow. A high score cannot compensate for violating one of these invariants.</p>
+        </aside>
+      </section>
+
+      <section class="chapter-section idea-cycle" id="mastery">
+        <span class="section-number">12</span>
+        <h2 class="section-title">Cumulative mastery · consistency is the force multiplier</h2>
+        <p class="section-lead">Recognition is not mastery. Close the chapter, rebuild the staircase from memory, classify unfamiliar prompts by capability, and explain why becoming bored with your own format is evidence that the interface is working.</p>
+
+        <div class="move move--hook">
+          <p class="move-label">1 · Hook — novelty tax</p>
+          <h3>Every bespoke prompt makes the trifecta learn a new language</h3>
+          <p>One prompt calls the main steps “Instructions,” another hides them below “Notes,” a third uses “Process,” and a fourth mixes the report contract into its final step. Each may work once. Together they form a library that cannot be scanned, compared, or generated reliably. Every prompt repays the same interpretation tax.</p>
+        </div>
+
+        <div class="move move--picture">
+          <p class="move-label">2 · Picture — predictable shape</p>
+          <h3>Same blocks, different capability stacks</h3>
+          <div class="format-strip" aria-label="Seven levels as one consistent prompt language">
+            <article style="--level-color:var(--level-1)"><b>1</b><strong>Request</strong><p>Save the repeat.</p></article>
+            <article style="--level-color:var(--level-2)"><b>2</b><strong>Sequence</strong><p>Make work executable.</p></article>
+            <article style="--level-color:var(--level-3)"><b>3</b><strong>Decision</strong><p>Branch and repeat.</p></article>
+            <article style="--level-color:var(--level-4)"><b>4</b><strong>Delegation</strong><p>Move context between agents.</p></article>
+            <article style="--level-color:var(--level-5)"><b>5</b><strong>Consume</strong><p>Pass prompt-like input.</p></article>
+            <article style="--level-color:var(--level-6)"><b>6</b><strong>Generate</strong><p>Instantiate a format.</p></article>
+            <article style="--level-color:var(--level-7)"><b>7</b><strong>Improve</strong><p>Update knowledge safely.</p></article>
+          </div>
+        </div>
+
+        <div class="move move--story">
+          <p class="move-label">3 · Story — the coworker test</p>
+          <h3>Could someone complete the work cold?</h3>
+          <p>Dan’s practical quality test is whether a coworker could take the prompt and complete the work from top to bottom. The test includes the agent: the Workflow must become a plan without private interpretation. A library passes when collapsed headings are familiar, variables have predictable placement, control flow is visible, and reports expose completion.</p>
+        </div>
+
+        <div class="move move--name">
+          <p class="move-label">4 · Name it</p>
+          <h3>Consistency is king</h3>
+          <aside class="callout callout--term"><p class="callout__label">The closing principle</p><p><strong>Consistency</strong> is the greatest weapon against confusion for you, your team, and your agents. Boredom is a positive signal: the format has become predictable enough that attention can move from finding the interface to judging the work.</p></aside>
+        </div>
+
+        <div class="move move--example">
+          <p class="move-label">5 · Worked example — one change, three readers</p>
+          <h3>Move <code>specs/</code> without rewriting the play</h3>
+          <p><code>quick-plan.md</code> exposes <code>PLAN_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY</code> as a static value. The author changes the operational destination once. A teammate recognizes the Variables convention. The agent resolves references inside the Workflow. When the metadata description remains stale, the mismatch is visible and reviewable because Metadata and Variables have distinct jobs.</p>
+        </div>
+
+        <div class="move move--try">
+          <p class="move-label">6 · You try — two-minute cold review</p>
+          <h3>Collapse before you read</h3>
+          <p>Pick an unfamiliar course command. Collapse it to headings, predict its level and inputs, then expand it and test your prediction. If the expanded text surprises you, identify whether the prompt violated the shared vocabulary or your mental map is incomplete.</p>
+        </div>
+
+        <div class="move move--fail">
+          <p class="move-label">7 · Common fail + fix</p>
+          <h3>Failure: consistency becomes cargo cult</h3>
+          <p><strong>Symptom:</strong> every prompt contains thirteen empty or redundant sections because “this is the standard.” The format becomes longer, not clearer.</p>
+          <p><strong>Fix:</strong> standardize names and responsibilities, not compulsory presence. The highest form of consistency is predictable omission: everyone understands that no Variables means nothing enters and no Report means no special response contract is required.</p>
+        </div>
+
+        <div class="move move--current">
+          <p class="move-label">8 · Current practice — portable conventions</p>
+          <h3>Consistency is what lets packaging evolve</h3>
+          <p>A stable vocabulary makes it easier to move reusable behavior from commands into skills, generate new artifacts with metaprompts, and compare prompt libraries across tools. The package can change because the underlying interface is coherent.</p>
+        </div>
+
+        <div class="move move--check">
+          <p class="move-label">9 · Retrieval — no notes, one sitting</p>
+          <section class="retrieval-quiz" aria-label="Cumulative seven-level quiz">
+            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">1. Name the seven levels and the single capability each adds.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>High Level—save a reusable request; Workflow—add sequential work; Control Flow—add conditions/loops/early returns; Delegate—launch other agents; Higher Order—accept another prompt/plan/file; Template Metaprompt—generate a prompt in a specified format; Self-Improving—update Expertise over time.</p></details></div>
+            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">2. What portion of ordinary work do Levels 1–4 cover in the lesson?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Roughly 80–90%; usually Level 3 or 4 is enough.</p></details></div>
+            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">3. Name all thirteen sections.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Title, High Level Prompt, Metadata, Purpose, Variables, Instructions, Relevant Files, Codebase Structure, Workflow, Expertise, Template, Examples, Report.</p></details></div>
+            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">4. Why are there thirteen when older text says twelve?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>The canonical app entity list includes High Level Prompt as its own section; the older prose predates that split and is documentation drift.</p></details></div>
+            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">5. Distinguish Workflow from Instructions.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Workflow is the ordered executable play; Instructions are auxiliary guardrails supporting that play.</p></details></div>
+            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">6. Distinguish Codebase Structure from Relevant Files.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Codebase Structure is a location map not read wholesale; Relevant Files names the files the agent should open.</p></details></div>
+            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">7. Give one real dynamic and one real static variable.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p><code>USER_PROMPT: $ARGUMENTS</code> is dynamic; <code>PLAN_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY: specs/</code> is static in <code>quick-plan.md</code>.</p></details></div>
+            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">8. Which section and format occupy S/S?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p><code>## Template</code> and Level-6 <code>template_metaprompt.md</code>.</p></details></div>
+            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">9. Which format is S/A, and why does it cost A skill?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Delegate Prompt; context, independence, agent prompts, collisions, outputs, and synthesis must all be engineered.</p></details></div>
+            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">10. Explain L5, L6, and L7 with one verb each.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>L5 consumes, L6 generates, L7 improves.</p></details></div>
+            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">11. What Level-7 invariant must never drift?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>The stable Workflow; the improve prompt updates only Expertise.</p></details></div>
+            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">12. Why do tier-list grades not transfer directly to system prompts?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>They grade task-local user prompts. System prompts have conversation-wide scope and persistence, so section value and acceptable rigidity change.</p></details></div>
+            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">13. Why can absence of a section be good design?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Sections are capability blocks. If the job has no input or required report shape, Variables or Report would add ceremony without capability.</p></details></div>
+            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">14. What does the coworker test assess?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Whether another person could pick up the prompt cold and complete its work top to bottom—an effective proxy for a clear agent-executable interface.</p></details></div>
+            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">15. Why is boredom a positive signal?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Predictable structure means the trifecta no longer spends attention rediscovering the interface; attention can move to judgment and outcomes.</p></details></div>
+          </section>
+        </div>
+
+        <div class="move move--teach">
+          <p class="move-label">10 · Teach-back — capstone</p>
+          <div class="teach-back">
+            <p><strong>Five-minute board talk, no notes.</strong></p>
+            <ol>
+              <li>Draw the seven-step staircase and name the capability gained at each step.</li>
+              <li>Draw Variables → Workflow → Report and explain why blocks are optional.</li>
+              <li>Place Workflow, Template, Delegate, and Self-Improving on the usefulness/skill grid.</li>
+              <li>Use <code>build.md</code> to demonstrate stacked Levels 2, 3, and 5.</li>
+              <li>End by contrasting a user command with a system prompt and resolving the boredom paradox.</li>
+            </ol>
+          </div>
+        </div>
+      </section>
+
+      <section class="chapter-section" id="glossary">
+        <span class="section-number">13</span>
+        <h2 class="section-title">Glossary</h2>
+        <p class="section-lead">Use these terms as a shared vocabulary when reviewing prompt libraries. The point is not jargon; it is to make capability, scope, and failure discussable.</p>
+        <dl class="glossary">
+          <div><dt>Agentic prompt</dt><dd>A prompt that can drive a multi-step agent/tool workflow rather than only generate a reply.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>Stakeholder Trifecta</dt><dd>You, your team, and your agents—the three readers a reusable prompt must serve.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>Composable section</dt><dd>A consistently named prompt region with one recognizable job that can be included or omitted as needed.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>High Level Prompt</dt><dd>A reusable, detail-light request; the required core of Level 1.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>Workflow</dt><dd>The ordered, executable play that maps the requested work into steps.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>Control flow</dt><dd>Conditions, loops, and early returns that make alternate paths explicit inside Workflow.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>Early return</dt><dd>A branch that stops execution when a prerequisite is missing or a termination condition is met.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>Delegate Prompt</dt><dd>A Level-4 prompt that authors work for other agents, launches them, and synthesizes their outputs.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>Higher Order Prompt</dt><dd>A Level-5 prompt that accepts another prompt, plan, or prompt-like file as input.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>Template Metaprompt</dt><dd>A Level-6 prompt that generates a new prompt according to a specified format.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>Self-Improving Prompt</dt><dd>A Level-7 pattern that updates embedded domain Expertise while preserving stable procedure.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>Dynamic variable</dt><dd>A value supplied at invocation time, such as <code>$1</code>, <code>$2</code>, or <code>$ARGUMENTS</code>.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>Static variable</dt><dd>A named value stored in the prompt and changed in one place, such as an output directory.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>Report</dt><dd>The output structure and completion evidence expected after Workflow finishes.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>Instructions</dt><dd>Auxiliary behavioral rules that support but do not replace the Workflow.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>Codebase Structure</dt><dd>A repository map used to locate context without implying that every listed file should be read.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>Relevant Files</dt><dd>A bounded set of files the agent is expected to open for the task.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>Expertise</dt><dd>Embedded domain knowledge consumed by a prompt and, in Level 7, updated over time.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>Template</dt><dd>An explicit output skeleton with placeholders that constrains generated artifacts.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>User prompt</dt><dd>A task-local request entering the current conversation, including the lesson’s slash commands.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>System prompt</dt><dd>Persistent instructions that define an agent’s role and behavior across all user prompts in a conversation.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>Scope and persistence</dt><dd>The dimensions that make system prompts more consequential than one task-local user prompt.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>Prompt library</dt><dd>A reusable, battle-tested collection of consistent prompt artifacts rather than disposable chat fragments.</dd></div>
+          <div><dt>Consistency</dt><dd>Stable names and section responsibilities that reduce interpretation cost across the trifecta.</dd></div>
+        </dl>
+      </section>
+
+      <footer class="chapter-footer">
+        <p class="eyebrow">Volume II · Agentic Horizon</p>
+        <div class="chapter-footer__nav">
+          <a href="../index.html">← Book hub</a>
+          <a href="../index.html">Next: AH-3 · Building Domain-Specific Agents →</a>
+        </div>
+      </footer>
+    </main>
+  </div>
+
+  <script>
+    (() => {
+      const topBar = document.getElementById('top-progress');
+      const railBar = document.getElementById('rail-progress');
+      const label = document.getElementById('progress-label');
+      const links = [...document.querySelectorAll('.chapter-nav a')];
+      const sections = links.map(link => document.querySelector(link.getAttribute('href'))).filter(Boolean);
+      let progressFramePending = false;
+
+      const updateProgress = () => {
+        const max = document.documentElement.scrollHeight - window.innerHeight;
+        const value = max > 0 ? Math.min(1, Math.max(0, window.scrollY / max)) : 0;
+        const percent = `${Math.round(value * 100)}%`;
+        if (topBar) topBar.style.width = percent;
+        if (railBar) railBar.style.width = percent;
+        if (label) label.textContent = percent;
+      };
+
+      const requestProgressUpdate = () => {
+        if (progressFramePending) return;
+        progressFramePending = true;
+        requestAnimationFrame(() => {
+          updateProgress();
+          progressFramePending = false;
+        });
+      };
+
+      if ('IntersectionObserver' in window) {
+        const observer = new IntersectionObserver(entries => {
+          const visible = entries.filter(entry => entry.isIntersecting).sort((a, b) => b.intersectionRatio - a.intersectionRatio)[0];
+          if (!visible) return;
+          links.forEach(link => {
+            const active = link.getAttribute('href') === `#${visible.target.id}`;
+            if (active) link.setAttribute('aria-current', 'location');
+            else link.removeAttribute('aria-current');
+          });
+        }, { rootMargin: '-20% 0px -65% 0px', threshold: [0, .1, .5] });
+        sections.forEach(section => observer.observe(section));
+      }
+
+      updateProgress();
+      window.addEventListener('scroll', requestProgressUpdate, { passive: true });
+      window.addEventListener('resize', requestProgressUpdate);
+    })();
+  </script>
+</body>
+</html>

diff --git a/IndyDevDan/book/vol-2-ah/10-seven-levels-agentic-prompt-formats.assets.css b/IndyDevDan/book/vol-2-ah/10-seven-levels-agentic-prompt-formats.assets.css
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a280e7ce6197318398d30da01a1d1397db864498
--- /dev/null
+++ b/IndyDevDan/book/vol-2-ah/10-seven-levels-agentic-prompt-formats.assets.css
@@ -0,0 +1,281 @@
+/* AH-2 reuses the TAC-1 gold grammar and adds prompt-format teaching visuals. */
+@import url("../vol-1-tac/01-hello-agentic-coding.assets.css");
+
+:root {
+  --chapter-wide: 68.75rem;
+  --level-1: #8a6a45;
+  --level-2: #a55a22;
+  --level-3: #a33d2e;
+  --level-4: #8a3f06;
+  --level-5: #5f536e;
+  --level-6: #3d6b56;
+  --level-7: #2f5d68;
+}
+
+.hero--prompts {
+  background:
+    linear-gradient(120deg, transparent 0 57%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-wash) 78%, transparent) 57% 100%),
+    var(--bg-card);
+}
+
+.hero--prompts::after { display: none; }
+
+.hero-stack {
+  display: grid;
+  grid-template-columns: repeat(7, minmax(0, 1fr));
+  gap: .45rem;
+  width: min(100%, 58rem);
+  margin-top: var(--space-7);
+  align-items: end;
+}
+
+.hero-stack__level {
+  display: grid;
+  place-items: end center;
+  min-height: calc(7rem + var(--i) * 1.35rem);
+  padding: .7rem .4rem;
+  border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 62%, var(--border));
+  border-radius: var(--radius-md) var(--radius-md) 0 0;
+  color: var(--accent-ink);
+  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-wash) calc(40% + var(--i) * 6%), var(--bg-card));
+  text-align: center;
+}
+
+.hero-stack__level b { display: block; font: 700 var(--text-lg)/1 var(--font-display); }
+.hero-stack__level span { display: block; margin-top: .4rem; font-size: var(--text-xs); line-height: 1.25; }
+
+.section-grid,
+.audience-grid,
+.choice-grid,
+.practice-grid,
+.proof-grid,
+.confusion-grid,
+.lab-evidence,
+.level-cards,
+.prompt-scope,
+.format-strip {
+  display: grid;
+  gap: var(--space-3);
+  width: 100%;
+  max-width: min(100%, var(--chapter-wide));
+  margin-inline: auto;
+}
+
+.section-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
+.audience-grid,
+.choice-grid,
+.proof-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
+.practice-grid,
+.confusion-grid,
+.prompt-scope { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
+.lab-evidence { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
+.level-cards { grid-template-columns: repeat(7, minmax(8.5rem, 1fr)); overflow-x: auto; padding-bottom: var(--space-2); }
+
+.section-grid article,
+.audience-grid article,
+.choice-grid article,
+.practice-grid article,
+.proof-grid article,
+.confusion-grid article,
+.lab-evidence article,
+.level-cards article,
+.prompt-scope article {
+  padding: var(--space-4);
+  border: var(--hairline);
+  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
+  background: var(--bg-card);
+  box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
+}
+
+.section-grid article { border-top: 4px solid var(--ink-mute); }
+.section-grid article:nth-child(4n + 1) { border-top-color: var(--accent); }
+.section-grid strong,
+.audience-grid strong,
+.choice-grid strong,
+.practice-grid strong,
+.proof-grid strong,
+.confusion-grid strong,
+.lab-evidence strong,
+.level-cards strong,
+.prompt-scope strong {
+  display: block;
+  color: var(--accent-ink);
+  font-family: var(--font-display);
+}
+
+.section-grid p,
+.audience-grid p,
+.choice-grid p,
+.practice-grid p,
+.proof-grid p,
+.confusion-grid p,
+.lab-evidence p,
+.level-cards p,
+.prompt-scope p { margin-top: var(--space-2); color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: var(--text-sm); }
+
+.audience-grid article:nth-child(3) { border-color: var(--accent); background: var(--accent-wash); }
+
+.level-staircase {
+  display: grid;
+  gap: .4rem;
+  width: 100%;
+  max-width: min(100%, var(--chapter-wide));
+  margin-inline: auto;
+  padding: var(--space-5);
+  border: var(--hairline);
+  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
+  background: var(--bg-card);
+  box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
+}
+
+.level-step {
+  display: grid;
+  grid-template-columns: 4.1rem minmax(11rem, .65fr) minmax(0, 1.35fr) 5.2rem;
+  gap: var(--space-3);
+  align-items: center;
+  width: calc(58% + var(--i) * 6%);
+  min-height: 4.5rem;
+  padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
+  border-left: .42rem solid var(--level-color);
+  border-radius: 0 var(--radius-md) var(--radius-md) 0;
+  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--level-color) 9%, var(--bg-card));
+}
+
+.level-step__n { color: var(--level-color); font: 750 var(--text-xl)/1 var(--font-display); }
+.level-step strong { color: var(--ink); font-family: var(--font-display); }
+.level-step p { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: var(--text-sm); }
+.level-step__grade { justify-self: end; color: var(--level-color); font: 750 var(--text-sm) var(--font-mono); }
+
+.flow-lens {
+  display: grid;
+  grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr;
+  gap: var(--space-3);
+  align-items: stretch;
+  width: 100%;
+  max-width: min(100%, var(--chapter-wide));
+  margin-inline: auto;
+  padding: clamp(1.2rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
+  border: 1px solid var(--accent);
+  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
+  background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--bg-card), var(--accent-wash));
+  box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
+}
+
+.flow-lens__block { display: grid; align-content: center; min-height: 12rem; padding: var(--space-4); border: var(--hairline); border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--bg-card); text-align: center; }
+.flow-lens__block b { color: var(--accent-ink); font: 650 var(--text-lg)/1.1 var(--font-display); }
+.flow-lens__block code { margin-top: var(--space-2); }
+.flow-lens__block p { margin-top: var(--space-3); color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: var(--text-sm); }
+.flow-lens__arrow { display: grid; place-items: center; color: var(--accent); font: 750 var(--text-xl) var(--font-display); }
+
+.prompt-snippet {
+  width: 100%;
+  max-width: min(100%, var(--chapter-wide));
+  margin-inline: auto;
+  padding: var(--space-5);
+  border: var(--hairline);
+  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
+  background: var(--bg-code);
+}
+.prompt-snippet pre { margin: 0; border: 0; padding: 0; white-space: pre-wrap; }
+.prompt-snippet__note { margin-top: var(--space-3); color: var(--ink-mute); font-size: var(--text-sm); }
+
+.tier-figure { width: 100%; max-width: min(100%, var(--chapter-wide)); margin-inline: auto; }
+.tier-grid {
+  display: grid;
+  grid-template-columns: 5.7rem repeat(5, minmax(8rem, 1fr));
+  overflow-x: auto;
+  border: 1px solid var(--border);
+  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
+  background: var(--bg-card);
+  box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
+}
+
+.tier-cell {
+  min-height: 8.2rem;
+  padding: var(--space-3);
+  border-right: var(--hairline);
+  border-bottom: var(--hairline);
+  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--cell-color, var(--bg-card)) 7%, var(--bg-card));
+}
+.tier-cell--axis { display: grid; place-items: center; min-height: 4rem; color: var(--ink-soft); background: var(--bg-inset); font: 700 var(--text-sm) var(--font-mono); text-align: center; }
+.tier-cell--row { color: var(--accent-ink); font-size: var(--text-xs); font-weight: 750; text-transform: uppercase; }
+.tier-pill { display: block; width: fit-content; margin: .28rem 0; padding: .25rem .45rem; border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 32%, var(--border)); border-radius: 999px; color: var(--ink); background: var(--bg-card); font-size: var(--text-xs); line-height: 1.25; }
+.tier-pill--format { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent-ink); font-weight: 750; }
+
+.format-strip { grid-template-columns: repeat(7, minmax(8.5rem, 1fr)); overflow-x: auto; }
+.format-strip article { min-height: 12rem; padding: var(--space-3); border-top: .38rem solid var(--level-color); border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--level-color) 8%, var(--bg-card)); }
+.format-strip b { display: block; color: var(--level-color); font: 750 var(--text-lg)/1 var(--font-display); }
+.format-strip strong { display: block; margin-top: var(--space-2); font-family: var(--font-display); }
+.format-strip p { margin-top: var(--space-2); color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: var(--text-xs); }
+
+.scope-axis {
+  position: relative;
+  width: 100%;
+  max-width: min(100%, var(--chapter-wide));
+  margin-inline: auto;
+  padding: var(--space-6);
+  border: var(--hairline);
+  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
+  background: var(--bg-card);
+}
+.scope-axis__line { height: .5rem; margin: var(--space-6) 2rem var(--space-2); border-radius: 999px; background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--ok), var(--accent), var(--warn)); }
+.scope-axis__labels { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--space-4); color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: var(--text-sm); }
+
+.decision-table { overflow-x: auto; width: 100%; max-width: min(100%, var(--chapter-wide)); margin-inline: auto; border: var(--hairline); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); background: var(--bg-card); }
+.decision-table table { min-width: 52rem; }
+
+.rubric-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.35fr repeat(4, minmax(7rem, .75fr)); width: 100%; max-width: min(100%, var(--chapter-wide)); margin-inline: auto; overflow: hidden; border: var(--hairline); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); background: var(--bg-card); }
+.rubric-grid > div { padding: var(--space-3); border-right: var(--hairline); border-bottom: var(--hairline); }
+.rubric-grid .rubric-head { color: var(--accent-ink); background: var(--accent-wash); font-weight: 750; }
+
+.lab-checklist { padding: 0; list-style: none; }
+.lab-checklist li { position: relative; padding-left: 2rem; }
+.lab-checklist li::before { position: absolute; left: 0; content: "□"; color: var(--accent-ink); font: 700 1.25rem var(--font-mono); }
+
+.chapter-main .frame-card { width: min(68.75rem, calc(100vw - var(--rail-width) - var(--space-8) - 4rem)); max-width: none; }
+.frame-card img { width: 100%; max-width: 68.75rem; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; object-fit: contain; background: var(--bg-card); }
+.frame-card figcaption { max-width: none; }
+.frame-sequence { display: grid; gap: var(--space-6); width: 100%; max-width: min(100%, var(--chapter-wide)); margin-inline: auto; }
+
+.teach-back { width: 100%; max-width: min(100%, var(--chapter-wide)); margin-inline: auto; }
+.source-note { padding: var(--space-4); border-left: 4px solid var(--ink-mute); background: var(--bg-inset); color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: var(--text-sm); }
+.graded-badge { display: inline-flex; padding: .2rem .55rem; border-radius: 999px; color: var(--ok); background: var(--ok-wash); font-size: var(--text-xs); font-weight: 750; letter-spacing: .05em; text-transform: uppercase; }
+
+@media (max-width: 72rem) {
+  .section-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
+  .audience-grid,
+  .choice-grid,
+  .proof-grid,
+  .lab-evidence { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
+  .level-step { width: 100%; }
+}
+
+@media (max-width: 52rem) {
+  .hero-stack { grid-template-columns: 1fr; align-items: stretch; }
+  .hero-stack__level { min-height: auto; place-items: center start; grid-template-columns: 2.5rem 1fr; text-align: left; }
+  .section-grid,
+  .practice-grid,
+  .confusion-grid,
+  .prompt-scope { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
+  .level-step { grid-template-columns: 3.2rem 1fr; }
+  .level-step p { grid-column: 2; }
+  .level-step__grade { grid-column: 2; justify-self: start; }
+  .flow-lens { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
+  .flow-lens__arrow { transform: rotate(90deg); }
+  .rubric-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
+  .rubric-grid > div { border-right: 0; }
+}
+
+@media print {
+  .hero-stack,
+  .level-staircase,
+  .flow-lens,
+  .tier-figure,
+  .prompt-scope,
+  .frame-card { break-inside: avoid; }
+  .level-step { width: 100%; }
+  .section-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
+  .tier-grid { grid-template-columns: 4.5rem repeat(5, 1fr); font-size: 8pt; }
+  .tier-cell { min-height: 5.7rem; padding: .35rem; }
+  .tier-pill { font-size: 7pt; }
+}
