579:          <div class="prompt-snippet"><pre><code>PROMPT_REQUEST: $1
657:            <img src="../media/frames/ah-2-seven-levels-agentic-prompt-formats/t2280-l6-metaprompt-specified-format.jpg" alt="Editor showing t_metaprompt_workflow.md with Documentation and Specified Format sections" width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy">
658:            <figcaption><span class="frame-card__t">38:00</span><code>t_metaprompt_workflow.md</code> combines <code>HIGH_LEVEL_PROMPT: $ARGUMENTS</code>, a Documentation map, and a Specified Format the agent must fill. The recording still says “follow the Instructions”; Dan corrects it live to “Workflow,” and the shipped file contains the correction.</figcaption>
967:            <article><strong>System prompt fit</strong><p>Purpose establishes identity. Instructions define broad behavior. Examples demonstrate patterns. A loose Workflow can orient without forcing every future task through one rigid sequence.</p></article>
969:          <div class="decision-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Section</th><th>User prompt</th><th>Primary-agent system prompt</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Purpose</td><td>Useful</td><td>Strong fit: role and identity</td></tr><tr><td>Instructions</td><td>Supporting guardrails</td><td>Strong fit: persistent behavior</td></tr><tr><td>Examples</td><td>Useful demonstrations</td><td>Strong fit: behavioral patterns</td></tr><tr><td>Workflow</td><td>Often deterministic</td><td>Keep loose to preserve agency</td></tr><tr><td>Variables / Report</td><td>Task-specific strengths</td><td>Usually avoid as global structure</td></tr><tr><td>Template / Expertise / Metadata</td><td>Useful in specific formats</td><td>Generally avoid in the broad primary system prompt</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
988:          <p><strong>Fix:</strong> re-evaluate by scope. Use Purpose, broad Instructions, and Examples to shape behavior. If a Workflow is present, keep it loose enough for many scenarios. Move deterministic task plays back into user prompts where they can be selected when relevant.</p>
1001:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">Name three strong system-prompt sections and three to avoid in a broad primary agent.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Strong: Purpose, Instructions, Examples, plus at most a loose Workflow. Avoid as general defaults: Variables, Report, Expertise/Template, Metadata, Relevant Files, and Codebase Structure.</p></details></div>
1074:            <li>Confirm the canonical count in <code>apps/prompt_tier_list/src/constants/entities.ts</code>: thirteen section strings followed by seven format strings.</li>
1116:            <li>In <code>quick-plan.md</code>, label line 14 <code>USER_PROMPT: $ARGUMENTS</code> dynamic and line 15 <code>PLAN_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY: specs/</code> static.</li>
1117:            <li>In <code>create_image.md</code>, label <code>IMAGE_GENERATION_PROMPT: $1</code> and <code>NUMBER_OF_IMAGES: $2</code> dynamic. Label <code>IMAGE_OUTPUT_DIR</code>, <code>MODEL</code>, and <code>ASPECT_RATIO</code> static.</li>
1151:            <li>Notice the shipped template’s purpose sentence mentions Instructions although the Specified Format does not include that H2. Grade the generated structure by the Workflow and Specified Format rules.</li>
1224:          <p><code>quick-plan.md</code> exposes <code>PLAN_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY</code> as a static value. The author changes the operational destination once. A teammate recognizes the Variables convention. The agent resolves references inside the Workflow. When the metadata description remains stale, the mismatch is visible and reviewable because Metadata and Variables have distinct jobs.</p>
